# Experiment 6 — Potentiometer Controlled LED Brightness

## Aim

To control LED brightness using potentiometer and Arduino UNO.

## Apparatus Required

* Arduino UNO
* Potentiometer
* LED
* 220Ω Resistor
* Breadboard
* Jumper Wires

## Pin Description

| Component                | Arduino Pin |
| ------------------------ | ----------- |
| Potentiometer Middle Pin | A0          |
| Potentiometer Side Pin   | 5V          |
| Potentiometer Other Side | GND         |
| LED                      | Pin 3       |

## Connection Diagram

```text id="c1e5dn"
Potentiometer Left ------- 5V

Potentiometer Middle ----- A0

Potentiometer Right ------ GND

LED ---------------------- Pin 3
```

## Program

```cpp
const int analog_in = A0;

void setup() {

  pinMode(3, OUTPUT);

  Serial.begin(115200);
}

void loop() {

  int val = analogRead(analog_in);

  analogWrite(3, val / 4);

  Serial.print("Potentiometer Value : ");
  Serial.println(val);

  delay(500);
}
```
