# Experiment 9 — Motor Control with Raspberry Pi

## Aim

To control DC motor using Raspberry Pi GPIO.

## Apparatus Required

* Raspberry Pi
* L293D Motor Driver
* DC Motor
* Jumper Wires

## Pin Description

| Raspberry Pi Physical Pin | GPIO   | L293D Connection |
| ------------------------- | ------ | ---------------- |
| Pin 11                    | GPIO17 | Input 1          |
| Pin 12                    | GPIO18 | Input 2          |
| Pin 2                     | 5V     | VCC              |
| Pin 6                     | GND    | GND              |

## Connection Diagram

```text id="0n53q3"
Raspberry Pi Pin 11 (GPIO17) ---- L293D IN1

Raspberry Pi Pin 12 (GPIO18) ---- L293D IN2

Raspberry Pi Pin 2 (5V) --------- L293D VCC

Raspberry Pi Pin 6 (GND) -------- L293D GND

L293D OUT1 and OUT2 ------------- DC Motor
```

## Program

```python id="mgl0a2"
from gpiozero import Motor
from time import sleep

motor = Motor(forward=17, backward=18)

print("Motor Forward")

motor.forward()

sleep(5)

print("Motor Stop")

motor.stop()
```

