# Experiment 14 — Real Time Data Visualization in ThingsBoard

## Aim

To visualize real-time sensor data using ThingsBoard.

## Apparatus Required

* Raspberry Pi
* DHT11 Sensor
* Internet Connection
* ThingsBoard Platform
* Jumper Wires

## Pin Description

| Raspberry Pi Physical Pin | GPIO  | DHT11 Pin |
| ------------------------- | ----- | --------- |
| Pin 1                     | 3.3V  | VCC       |
| Pin 7                     | GPIO4 | DATA      |
| Pin 6                     | GND   | GND       |

## Connection Diagram

```text id="3mkt4g"
Raspberry Pi Pin 1 (3.3V) ---- DHT11 VCC

Raspberry Pi Pin 7 (GPIO4) --- DHT11 DATA

Raspberry Pi Pin 6 (GND) ----- DHT11 GND

Raspberry Pi ---- Internet ---- ThingsBoard Cloud
```

## Program

```python id="zpw9j3"
import adafruit_dht
import board
import paho.mqtt.client as mqtt
import json
import time

BROKER = "thingsboard.cloud"
PORT = 1883

ACCESS_TOKEN = "YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN"

# DHT11 Sensor
dht = adafruit_dht.DHT11(board.D4)

# MQTT Client
client = mqtt.Client()

client.username_pw_set(ACCESS_TOKEN)

client.connect(BROKER, PORT, 60)

client.loop_start()

print("Sending DHT11 data to ThingsBoard...")

while True:

    try:

        temperature = dht.temperature
        humidity = dht.humidity

        if temperature is not None and humidity is not None:

            payload = {
                "temperature": temperature,
                "humidity": humidity
            }

            client.publish(
                "v1/devices/me/telemetry",
                json.dumps(payload)
            )

            print("Sent:", payload)

        else:

            print("Sensor Read Failed")

    except RuntimeError as e:

        print("Retrying Sensor...", e.args[0])

    time.sleep(5)
```

## Output

```text id="ntn9fp"
Connected to ThingsBoard

Sending DHT11 data...

Sent:
Temperature = 29°C
Humidity = 68%
```

## Result

Real-time sensor data visualization was successfully implemented using ThingsBoard.

